        "\n",
        "## 📦 Part 1: What is an Array / List?\n",
        "\n",
        "Imagine you are managing an online game inventory, a class record, or a music playlist.\n",
        "- **Without Arrays:** You would need separate variables like `item1 = \"Notebook\"`, `item2 = \"Pen\"`, `item3 = \"Calculator\"`, etc. This gets messy very quickly!\n",
        "- **With Arrays / Lists:** You can group all related items into **one single variable**:\n",
        "  ```python\n",
        "  backpack = [\"Notebook\", \"Pen\", \"Calculator\", \"Laptop\", \"Book\"]\n",
        "  ```\n",
        "\n",
        "### 💡 Real-World Analogy: A Row of Boxes\n",
        "Think of a list as a row of numbered boxes sitting on a shelf. Each box holds **one item**, and each box has a position number called an **index**.\n",
