        "---\n",
        "## ✂️ Part 4: List Slicing & Searching\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. List Slicing (`list[start:end]`)\n",
        "Slicing allows you to extract a sub-list (a portion of your list).\n",
        "- Syntax: `list_name[start:end]`\n",
        "- **Remember:** The slice starts at `start` index and goes up to, but **does NOT include**, `end` index!\n",
        "- Example: `backpack[1:4]` gets items at index 1, 2, and 3.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Linear Searching\n",
        "Searching means checking if a target value exists in your list and finding its index position."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "kcgAXeQduIm7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Slicing and Searching Demo (Matching Activity 2 Requirements)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Reset list\n",
        "backpack = [\"Notebook\", \"Pen\", \"Tablet\", \"Laptop\", \"Book\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Original Backpack List:\", backpack)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Extracting a sliced portion from index 1 to 4 (indexes 1, 2, 3)\n",
        "sliced_backpack = backpack[1:4]\n",
        "print(\"Sliced Sub-List (1:4):\", sliced_backpack)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Linear Search Function\n",
        "search_item = \"Laptop\"\n",
        "\n",
        "if search_item in sliced_backpack:\n",
        "    found_index = sliced_backpack.index(search_item)\n",
        "    print(f\"🔍 Search Result: '{search_item}' was found in the sliced list at sub-index {found_index}!\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(f\"🔍 Search Result: '{search_item}' was not found in the sliced list.\")\n"
      ]
